## Raster sidecar
Every record carries `raster` + top-level `gate_snn` + `gate_compute`. Windows {wins[0]:.0f}/{wins[1]:.0f}/{wins[2]:.0f} ms; `window_s == window_ms/1000` exactly; `spikes == round(neurons·rate·window_s)` with zero slack ({n_sp[0]}/{n_sp[1]}/{n_sp[2]} at {rates[0]}/{rates[1]}/{rates[2]} Hz over {n_neu[0]}/{n_neu[1]}/{n_neu[2]} neurons); `energy_pJ = spikes·23` and `energy_uJ = spikes·23e-6` exact ({n_sp[0]*23}/{n_sp[1]*23}/{n_sp[2]*23} pJ). Routing source/target + 3-entry tables + `third_factor` on all three (modulators {tfs[0]} / {tfs[1]} / {tfs[2]}; τe {taus[0]}/{taus[1]}/{taus[2]} s as consistent `tau_e_s`+`tau_e_ms` pairs). Excerpts integer `t_us`, in-window, `neuron_id`-bounded, sorted, full-window by construction, per-spike amplitude with adaptation (0.82**k) plus noise. ISI histograms from the full window, bins ≥1 ms, counts sum to `spikes − distinct_active_neurons` ({isis[0]}/{isis[1]}/{isis[2]}). Same-neuron gaps ≥1100 µs pre-round, ≥1000 µs serialized. `gate_snn` on all three: decisions REJECT/MODIFY/ACCEPT matching each lead trajectory; every rate-declaring population's budget exact against its decision window. `gate_compute.per_check` windows 32–40 ms, budgets exact ({gc[0]} / {gc[1]} / {gc[2]}). Main streams: {events[0]}/{events[1]}/{events[2]} events (inside the 5–40 cap), strictly increasing `t_rel_ms` only (no `t_ms` mix), same-channel refractory ≥0.8 ms (175 zirconia pair at 1.3 ms, 176 Rogowski pair at 1.2 ms, 177 BAM pair at 1.5 ms).

## Self-critique

### Edge cases added vs still thin
- **Added:** first zirconia-wideband-electrochemical-O2 family on a glass-furnace crown with a recomputable x=k_z·(I−I0) (`6.00 volpct`) plus pump-flow identity and three-party collusion including the ZRO infra owner; first Rogowski-coil family on an EAF bus with recomputable I=k_r·V/f (`20.00 kA`) and I·f identity, plus a resolved-innocent coil tech (timezone-skipped integrator-zero, not last-to-badge); first beta-attenuation-BAM family on a sinter baghouse with recomputable C=k_b·(I0−I)/Q (`24.00 mg/m3`) plus mass identity; bounded ACCEPT whose out-of-scope clause is adjacent baghouse compartments rather than a hopper/taphole/dump cap; operational t2 on all three (damper hold, new-coil restart, skip-compartment refusal); provenance trio designed/hil/simulated; 18 min / 24 min / 12 min slow floors in-stream.
- **Still thin:** (i) 175's k_z is a lumped mA→volpct gain, not a T/P/Nernst-slope table — a thermal hop that fakes 6.00 volpct inside a 0.80 Nernstveil corridor is unwritten; (ii) 176's k_r is a lumped coil factor, not a temperature/position map, so a V hop that fakes 20.00 kA is unwritten; (iii) 177's k_b is a lumped beta-attenuation factor, not a humidity / tape-mass table, so an I hop that fakes 24.00 mg/m3 inside a 4.80 last-good is unwritten; (iv) vendor-only as a *lead* REJECT on a plant with *no* independent zirconia/Rogowski/BAM installed yet remains slightly harder — 175/176 still have plant heads; (v) stream amplitudes remain authored constants (raster draws are the only seeded noise); (vi) r46 densification leftovers (T/P susceptibility, wedge-delay map, TEOM Q-bias) and r31 two-color LII leftover were left for those rounds' owners.

### Realism of noise / temporal fidelity
- Strong: 175's 6.00 volpct, pump-flow identity 6.00, and 18.0 min damper-hold (`6000+1080=7080 s`) recompute from the record; 176's 20.00 kA, I·f 1000.00, and 24.0 min cooldown (`2820+1440=4260 s`) recompute; 177's 24.00 mg/m3, mass 48.00 ug, and 12.0 min survey (`6000+720=6720 s`) recompute. Raster adaptation (0.82**k plus 4% noise) and the 1.2–1.5 ms physics pairs give the 5–40 stream a raster-scale motif without violating 0.8 ms same-channel refractory.
- **Gaps, honestly:** (i) 5–40 cap still forces heavy thinning (10 Hz zirconia pump kept as 4 I points; kHz Rogowski kept as 4 V points plus one f pair; 1 Hz BAM kept as 4 I points); (ii) 175's post-stop 3.20 volpct is a later sample, not a closed-loop damper controller; (iii) 176 HIL coupon times an in-service isolate that the stream does not independently witness on a second live bus until the new coil starts; (iv) no gate_snn input→output volley pair at raster resolution this round (r04-a1 already staged that).

### Training value (SNN/LSM + agentic)
Distillation targets: zirconia x=k_z·(I−I0) reconstruction head plus pump-flow identity; conjunctive oxidizing floor vs continue-firing vs tank ESD; ZRO-infra collusion; Rogowski I=k_r·V/f head plus I·f identity; isolate-floor bus vs keep-arcing vs shop-trip; exoneration against last-to-badge social pressure; BAM C=k_b·(I0−I)/Q and mass identities; bounded ACCEPT with compartment-out-of-scope; skip-isolate refusal under survey takt. Agentic value concentrates in three patterns: reconstruction-as-SoT on a physical O2/current/PM load the raw corridor cannot see, earned ACCEPT with an explicit physical out-of-scope object (C-1..C-5), and stop-then-hold so a REJECT does not become a tank/shop/stack kill.

## What a later leftover-mill round should add (next densification target)
1. **T/P/Nernst-slope table** on a non-GH-6 crown so a thermal hop fakes 6.00 volpct inside a 0.80 Nernstveil corridor, closing 175's lumped-k_z gap.
2. **Coil-temperature / position map** on a non-DH-8 bus so a V hop can fake 20.00 kA while mean voltage looks healthy.
3. **Humidity / tape-mass table** on a non-OH-6 BAM so an I hop can fake 24.00 mg/m3 inside a 4.80 last-good corridor.
4. **Vendor-only as a lead REJECT** on a plant that has no independent zirconia/Rogowski/BAM installed yet (175/176 still had plant heads).
